\begin{example} %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%% EXAMPLE BOX
A mixture of 2 mol of \ce{N_2} and 2 mol of \ce{H_2} was placed in a 2L vessel at 720$^{\circ}$C. At that temperature, the equilibrium constant for the formation of ammonia is $K_c$=2.4$\times 10^{-3}$
\begin{center} \ce{H_2_{(g)} + 3H_2_{(g)} <=> 2NH_3_{(g)}    }
\end{center}
Once the equilibrium is reached, calculate the equilibrium concentration of the reactants and products.
\\
\textlcsc{ \textcolor{dgreen}{\Large \textbf{Solution}} }\\
We will first build up the ICE chart given that the initial concentration of reactants is both 1M

\begin{center}\begin{tikzpicture}
 \node[inner sep=0pt] (tab){%
 \begin{tabular}{l | l  l l ll}
       & \ce{N_2_{(g)}}  & + &3\ce{H_2_{(g)}} &  \ce{<=>}  &2\ce{NH_3_{(g)}}  \\
  \hline
  Initial     &1M  &&1M&&0M  \\
  Change    &$-x$  &&$-3x$&&$2x$    \\
  Equilibrium  &1$-x$  &&1$-3x$&&$2x$    \\
\end{tabular}
};
\node[draw=red, inner sep=0pt, rounded corners=3pt, line width=2pt,
fit=(tab.north west) (tab.north east) (tab.south east) (tab.south west)] {};
\end{tikzpicture}\end{center}
Now we will obtain the polynomial and solve for the extent. Using the expression for $K_c$
\[ \frac{  [\ce{NH3}]^2 }{[\ce{N2}] \cdot [\ce{H2}]^3}=K_c  \]
now substituting the values from the ICE chart:
\[ \frac{  (2x)^2 }{(1-x) \cdot (1-3x)^3}=K_c \ \]
By opening parenthesis we obtain 
\[  \frac{  4x^2 }{27x^4-54x^3+36x^2-10x+1}=K_c\]

The corresponding polynomial will be
\[27x^4-54x^3+(36-\frac{4}{K_c})x^2-10x+1=0   \]
The final polynomial will be
\[P(x)=27x^4-54x^3-1630.7x^2-10x+1=0   \]

By solving given that $K_c$=2.4$\times 10^{-3}$, we obtain four different roots, and only the positive root lower than one, $x=0.022$ has chemical sense. Mind that $x$ can not be smaller than the given initial concentration of 1M. The other roots are: 8.8, -0.028, and -6.83M. Now we can obtain the equilibrium concentrations for reactants and products: 
[\ce{N2}]=0.978M, [\ce{H2}]=0.934M, and [\ce{NH3}]=0.044M
based on the ICE chart
\begin{center}\begin{tikzpicture}
 \node[inner sep=0pt] (tab){%
 \begin{tabular}{l | l  l l ll}
       & \ce{N_2_{(g)}}  & + &3\ce{H_2_{(g)}} &  \ce{<=>}  &2\ce{NH_3_{(g)}}  \\
  \hline
  Initial     &1M  &&1M&&0M  \\
  Change    &$-0.022$  &&$-0.066$&&$0.044$    \\
  Equilibrium  &$0.978M$  &&$0.934M$&&$0.044M$    \\
\end{tabular}
};
\node[draw=red, inner sep=0pt, rounded corners=3pt, line width=2pt,
fit=(tab.north west) (tab.north east) (tab.south east) (tab.south west)] {};
\end{tikzpicture}\end{center}  
